sequenceDiagram
  accTitle: A shopper buys running shoes in Gemini: UCP checkout, an AP2 checkout mandate (per spec), Google Pay, signed order webhooks
  accDescr: Sequence diagram: A shopper buys running shoes in Gemini: UCP checkout, an AP2 checkout mandate (per spec), Google Pay, signed order webhooks. 7 participants: Shopper, Gemini (UCP platform, shopping agent), Trusted checkout UI (Trusted Surface), Google Pay (credential provider), Merchant (business, merchant of record), Merchant PSP (Merchant Payment Processor), and Card network and issuer. 14 steps, 10 crossing a trust boundary, 9 failure branches. Based on several protocols UCP v2026-08-25 AP2 v0.2 (2026-08-25). Step 1: Shopper to Gemini (UCP platform, shopping agent): Ask for running shoes. Step 2: Gemini (UCP platform, shopping agent) to Merchant (business, merchant of record): GET /.well-known/ucp (business profile). This step crosses a trust boundary. If The two profiles share no compatible capability: capabilities_incompatible (returned with HTTP 200 inside a UCP response). Step 3: Gemini (UCP platform, shopping agent) to Merchant (business, merchant of record): POST /checkout-sessions with UCP-Agent. This step crosses a trust boundary. Step 4: Merchant (business, merchant of record) to Gemini (UCP platform, shopping agent): Checkout with ap2.merchant_authorization. This step crosses a trust boundary. If The signature is missing or does not verify against the merchant's keys: merchant_authorization_missing or merchant_authorization_invalid the platform must not show the checkout. If The merchant needs buyer input it cannot get through the API: status requires_escalation with continue_url the shopper finishes on the merchant's site. Step 5: Gemini (UCP platform, shopping agent) to Trusted checkout UI (Trusted Surface): Verify the merchant signature, hand off to the trusted UI. This step crosses a trust boundary. Step 6: Shopper to Trusted checkout UI (Trusted Surface): Review and approve choose Google Pay. Step 7: Trusted checkout UI (Trusted Surface) to Google Pay (credential provider): Run the com.google.pay handler (PAN_ONLY). This step crosses a trust boundary. If The merchant's PSP cannot process Google's tokens: The merchant cannot accept this handler Google's FAQ makes PSP support a precondition. Step 8: Trusted checkout UI (Trusted Surface) to Trusted checkout UI (Trusted Surface): Create the closed mandates (per spec live use unverified). Step 9: Gemini (UCP platform, shopping agent) to Merchant (business, merchant of record): POST /checkout-sessions/ id /complete (signed, with ap2.checkout_mandate). This step crosses a trust boundary. If AP2 was negotiated but ap2.checkout_mandate is missing: mandate_required the merchant must reject the complete. If The response to complete is lost: Poll Get Checkout with bounded backoff and stop at expires_at only if the state is still unclear, resend the identical request with the same Idempotency-Key. During complete_in_progress the platform must not start a new update or complete. Step 10: Merchant (business, merchant of record) to Merchant (business, merchant of record): Verify the checkout mandate against the current checkout. If The mandate is for another checkout, expired or badly signed: mandate_scope_mismatch, mandate_expired or mandate_invalid_signature. Step 11: Merchant (business, merchant of record) to Merchant PSP (Merchant Payment Processor): Authorize the Google Pay token processor checks the payment mandate. This step crosses a trust boundary. Step 12: Merchant PSP (Merchant Payment Processor) to Card network and issuer: Card authorization. This step crosses a trust boundary. If The issuer declines: The merchant returns a payment failure in the checkout no order is created. Step 13: Merchant (business, merchant of record) to Gemini (UCP platform, shopping agent): completed with order receipts. This step crosses a trust boundary. Step 14: Merchant (business, merchant of record) to Gemini (UCP platform, shopping agent): Order webhook, RFC 9421 signed. This step crosses a trust boundary. If The webhook signer is not the order's business: The platform must reject the event.
  autonumber
  participant p_buyer as Shopper
  participant p_gemini as Gemini (UCP platform, shopping agent)
  participant p_surface as Trusted checkout UI (Trusted Surface)
  participant p_gpay as Google Pay (credential provider)
  participant p_merchant as Merchant (business, merchant of record)
  participant p_psp as Merchant PSP (Merchant Payment Processor)
  participant p_network as Card network and issuer
  p_buyer->>p_gemini: Ask for running shoes
  alt Expected path
    p_gemini->>p_merchant: GET /.well-known/ucp (business profile)
    Note over p_gemini,p_merchant: Crosses a trust boundary
  else The two profiles share no compatible capability
    Note over p_gemini,p_merchant: capabilities_incompatible (returned<br/>with HTTP 200 inside a UCP response).
  end
  p_gemini->>p_merchant: POST /checkout-sessions with UCP-Agent
  Note over p_gemini,p_merchant: Crosses a trust boundary
  alt Expected path
    p_merchant-->>p_gemini: Checkout with ap2.merchant_authorization
    Note over p_merchant,p_gemini: Crosses a trust boundary
  else The signature is missing or does not verify against the merchant#39;s keys
    Note over p_merchant,p_gemini: merchant_authorization_missing or<br/>merchant_authorization_invalid#59; the<br/>platform must not show the checkout.
  else The merchant needs buyer input it cannot get through the API
    Note over p_merchant,p_gemini: status requires_escalation with continue_url#59;<br/>the shopper finishes on the merchant#39;s site.
  end
  p_gemini->>p_surface: Verify the merchant signature,<br/>hand off to the trusted UI
  Note over p_gemini,p_surface: Crosses a trust boundary
  p_buyer->>p_surface: Review and approve#59; choose Google Pay
  alt Expected path
    p_surface->>p_gpay: Run the com.google.pay handler (PAN_ONLY)
    Note over p_surface,p_gpay: Crosses a trust boundary
  else The merchant#39;s PSP cannot process Google#39;s tokens
    Note over p_surface,p_gpay: The merchant cannot accept this handler#59;<br/>Google#39;s FAQ makes PSP support a precondition.
  end
  p_surface->>p_surface: Create the closed mandates (per<br/>spec#59; live use unverified)
  alt Expected path
    p_gemini->>p_merchant: POST /checkout-sessions/#123;id#125;/complete<br/>(signed, with ap2.checkout_mandate)
    Note over p_gemini,p_merchant: Crosses a trust boundary
  else AP2 was negotiated but ap2.checkout_mandate is missing
    Note over p_gemini,p_merchant: mandate_required#59; the merchant must reject the complete.
  else The response to complete is lost
    Note over p_gemini,p_merchant: Poll Get Checkout with bounded backoff and stop at expires_at#59;<br/>only if the state is still unclear, resend the identical request<br/>with the same Idempotency-Key. During complete_in_progress the<br/>platform must not start a new update or complete.
  end
  alt Expected path
    p_merchant->>p_merchant: Verify the checkout mandate<br/>against the current checkout
  else The mandate is for another checkout, expired or badly signed
    Note over p_merchant: mandate_scope_mismatch, mandate_expired<br/>or mandate_invalid_signature.
  end
  p_merchant->>p_psp: Authorize the Google Pay token#59;<br/>processor checks the payment mandate
  Note over p_merchant,p_psp: Crosses a trust boundary
  alt Expected path
    p_psp->>p_network: Card authorization
    Note over p_psp,p_network: Crosses a trust boundary
  else The issuer declines
    Note over p_psp,p_network: The merchant returns a payment failure<br/>in the checkout#59; no order is created.
  end
  p_merchant->>p_gemini: completed with order#59; receipts
  Note over p_merchant,p_gemini: Crosses a trust boundary
  alt Expected path
    p_merchant->>p_gemini: Order webhook, RFC 9421 signed
    Note over p_merchant,p_gemini: Crosses a trust boundary
  else The webhook signer is not the order#39;s business
    Note over p_merchant,p_gemini: The platform must reject the event.
  end
